# Evidence reports an attestation can pin.
#
# `legion attest` pins a source by the sha256 of its raw bytes and `legion ship`
# re-hashes them, deliberately without normalising line endings — see
# packages/cli/src/workflow/pinned-references.ts, whose pins were all minted raw.
# Without this rule these files check out CRLF on Windows and LF elsewhere, so an
# attestation minted on one platform reads `drift` on the other, and `drift` is
# the gates' strongest negative arm: a governance verdict would flip on a
# checkout setting. The index already holds LF, so this changes no committed blob.
docs/next/evidence/** text eol=lf
